body:
This is probably related to changes to CommentChecker and the type parse tree.

Using the latest version of upstream/master: Psalm warns that `-` is an undeclared class.

```php
<?php

/**
 * @return - Description (The hyphen is a hackish way to include a description but not a type. I suppress a warning about invalid docblocks here)
 */
function example() {
    return "placeholder";
}
```

Something similar to the below fix would fix these issues (my fork is slightly different):
I'm not sure if my fix covers every possible invalid union type.

```diff
@@ -99,9 +99,14 @@ abstract class Type
         $type_tokens = self::tokenize($type_string);
 
         if (count($type_tokens) === 1) {
-            $token = self::fixScalarTerms($type_tokens[0], $php_compatible);
+            $only_token = $type_tokens[0];
+            // Note: valid identifiers can include class names or $this
+            if (!preg_match('@^(\$this$|[a-zA-Z_\x7f-\xff])@', $only_token)) {
+                throw new TypeParseTreeException("Invalid type '$only_token'");
+            }
+            $only_token = self::fixScalarTerms($only_token, $php_compatible);
 
-            return new Union([Atomic::create($token, $php_compatible, $template_types)]);
+            return new Union([Atomic::create($only_token, $php_compatible, $template_types)]);
         }
```

Aside: Class names can be unicode (but those are not commonly used in my experience)
